cies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"When I move a PointLight with a camera I'm getting a following noisy output:\n![noise](https://f.cloud.github.com/assets/1032408/2038447/4cf3494c-898e-11e3-8eff-9cd5eab2ccf9.png)\n\nhttp://jsfiddle.net/Z6CVP/2/\n\nI suspect the problem is drivers specific. This happens on a Linux machine (Ubuntu 12.04) on both Chrome 31 and Firefox 26. On the same machine on Windows XP, the output is valid.\n\nThis is the first problem that I encountered with Three.js/webgl on this system, other demos look good with no noise.\n\nThis also worked correctly with older versions of Three.js. For example r56 produces nice output on the same machine:\n\n![nonoise](https://f.cloud.github.com/assets/1032408/2038446/4cf2c6de-898e-11e3-90d1-566714b37e04.png)\n\nhttp://jsfiddle.net/3Utnv/2/\n\nSome machine config info:\n\n```\nlspci | grep VGA\n01:00.0 VGA compatible controller: NVIDIA Corporation G96 [GeForce 9500 GT] (rev a1)\n\nglxinfo|g Ope\nOpenGL vendor string: NVIDIA Corporation\nOpenGL renderer string: GeForce 9500 GT/PCIe/SSE2\nOpenGL version string: 3.3.0 NVIDIA 304.88\nOpenGL shading language version string: 3.30 NVIDIA via Cg compiler\n```\n","closed_by":{"login":"mrdoob","id":97088,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3MDg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97088?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrdoob/event